{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/595201-what-does-it-take-to-start-a-new-tribe","id":595201,"title":"What does it take to start a new Tribe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T18:25:08-07:00","id":595201,"title":"What does it take to start a new Tribe?","content":"An idea that I had for a mini tribe (like the Siberakh) is one where a handful of Ronin and former BSDs who were cured of there corruption in the Erebus formed a mini tribe around the Dog Totem and are holed up at a small Caern dedicated to Stealth. Would spirits accept them, power their Rites, teach them Gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T18:41:46-07:00","id":595222,"title":"","content":"Probably. You can find spirits to do anything if you pay chiminage or happen to have qualities that they find appealing. They'd only be slightly more populous than the Singing Dogs, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T18:44:12-07:00","id":595226,"title":"","content":"You need three things to have a tribe: people, culture and a Tribe Totem.<br /> <br /> The Siberakh can be either an example of the bare minimum for a tribe to exist or even an anomaly, tough the Skin Dancers are also almost a tribe now. Or are they, I don't remember.<br /> <br /> Either way, work on those things. Have those guys get enough numbers and found a common cultural ground. Them they have to seek a Totem with enough power, or a totem with potential to obtain such power. Most tribes live in a symbiosis with their totens in that respect, the tribe being as much necessary for the totem as the totem is for the tribe.<br /> <br /> Curiously, the simplest tribe to come (back) into existence would be the most avoided, the White Howlers. They still have numbers and culture, (most BSD are culturaly corrupted WH) you only need to put enough of them together (no easy feat, sure) and raise the power of Lion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T19:06:32-07:00","id":595232,"title":"","content":"I don't see why it's not-viable in the setting as-is.<br /> <br /> The only thing to deal with is the implications of enough BSDs being successfully cleansed in Erebus to give this group some numbers. A successful BSD redemption is supposed to be a fairly major deal in-setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T19:24:20-07:00","id":595239,"title":"","content":"I think skin dancers can be considered a tribe. They do have a totem spirit now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T19:38:50-07:00","id":595242,"title":"","content":"Its that technicaly the totem isn't enough per se, but things are a little murky in the details. I know they have two totens already, but just one or two gifts.<br /> <br /> So, tough the requisites are simply those three I mentioned, it isn't easy to say when you have a tribe, when you have just a weird group.<br /> <br /> But I don't see any reason for that not to work, either. Probably the group will have a hard and long time forging alliances with spirits to build a half-decent corpus of Gifts and all. But by no means it would be impossible, its quite simple indeed, just hard to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T20:02:45-07:00","id":595251,"title":"","content":"If the yeren can do it.... And I mean those guys are pricks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:07:39-07:00","id":595959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/595201-what-does-it-take-to-start-a-new-tribe#post595201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea that I had for a mini tribe (like the Siberakh) is one where a handful of Ronin and former BSDs who were cured of there corruption in the Erebus formed a mini tribe around the Dog Totem and are holed up at a small Caern dedicated to Stealth. Would spirits accept them, power their Rites, teach them Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as they have a spirit patron spirits will teach them their auspice gifts, so as long as the Dog totem has accepted them then he will act as their emissary when dealing with spirits. Gifts taught by Dog spirits would obviously be the easiest for your tribe to learn at first. You will have to make alliances with other spirits or have those alliances established to have access to more gifts. Since they are allied with a spirit heavily associated with a domesticated animal you may be able to find other spirits that also benefit from co-existence with people, in the DA book it talks about Horse being such a totem that is no longer in the favor with the normal tribes so it might be willing to make an alliance. Spirits of the city that are common amongst the Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers might also be willing to make pacts with them.<br /> <br /> I think your new tribes greatest problem is going to be other tribes. Many of the old tribes are notorious for nonacceptance (like with the Siberahk). The Outcasts book gives a pretty good idea of how poorly Ronin are considered and ex-BSD willl not be looked at any more favorably so they should be careful to keep the tribes beginnings a secret.<br /> <br /> In another thread we were discussing new subtribes and tribes. I love coming with ideas like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:22:42-07:00","id":597088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/595201-what-does-it-take-to-start-a-new-tribe?p=595959#post595959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...so as long as the Dog totem has accepted them ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Off topic: Was Dog ever actually listed as a totem anywhere? (I never saw it, so I created a plot which revolved around Dog having been destroyed either during or shortly after the Impergium, and was wondering if I violated canon somehow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:42:54-07:00","id":597107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/595201-what-does-it-take-to-start-a-new-tribe?p=597088#post597088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off topic: Was Dog ever actually listed as a totem anywhere? (I never saw it, so I created a plot which revolved around Dog having been destroyed either during or shortly after the Impergium, and was wondering if I violated canon somehow).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hengeyokai, and commonly taken by Hakken (their tribe name is literally &quot;eight dogs&quot;, each of which represents a Confucian virtue) and Tengu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:26:31-07:00","id":597167,"title":"","content":"There are actually many Pariah/Wild Dog breeds (Carolina Dog, Dingo, Basenji, Indian Pariah, a couple others) and Domesticated Dogs still exist so having the totem would die out would be strange. As Saur has said, the totem is still alive and kicking in the East, often adopted by the Hakken and Tengu. He has come to embrace humanity, so most shifters want nothing to do with him. For him to have a western counterpart wouldn't be odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:04:00-07:00","id":597664,"title":"","content":"On a side note 626 I wouldn't worry about violating canon in wod. The devs seem to love the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T01:57:01-07:00","id":603679,"title":"","content":"There's also Dog as a caern totem in World of Rage.<br /> <br /> As for the question? it's pretty simple, all it takes is two things.<br /> <br /> 1) A group of Garou who are not already members of a tribe<br /> and<br /> 2) a single totem spirit to serve as their patron <i>beyond</i> the pack bond. <br /> <br /> That second part is obviously the tricky one, as you need <i>at least</i> an exceptionally powerful jaggling, or more likely an Incarna, to pick you up for that... and most of them are already &quot;spoken for.&quot; They're part of other totem's broods, they're tied to older, much more respected tribes, and so on. You would need to find a totem spirit who's either willing to risk their established hierarchy for you (good luck!) <i>or</i> find one that doesn't really have much of a place in the hierarchy (which tends to preclude the power you need.) The spirits who fit both bills are generally... unsavory or rather alien sorts, like, well... Tick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}